{#- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    page.html.j2 — generic singleton page wrapper.

    Renders a hand-authored page body through the shared base shell. The body
    and any head/script extras are supplied as raw HTML fragments living in
    _templates/pages/<key>.{body,styles,extra_scripts,tail_scripts}.html and
    loaded by build_pages() in build.py. Per-page metadata (title, heading,
    container class/style, whether the Optergy live-data libs are needed) comes
    from _data/pages.yaml.

    This is the catch-all for one-off pages that aren't driven by a data
    registry (building performance, landlord services, docs, the legacy
    verde-template floors 6–11, the report viewer scaffold, …). To edit one of
    these pages, edit its body fragment and rebuild — the shell stays central.
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block extra_styles %}{{ extra_styles_html|default('') }}{% endblock %}
{% block optergy_scripts %}{% if no_optergy|default(false) %}{% else %}{{ super() }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}{{ body|default('') }}{% endblock %}
{% block extra_scripts %}{{ extra_scripts_html|default('') }}{% endblock %}
{% block tail_scripts %}{{ tail_scripts_html|default('') }}{% endblock %}
